	"title": "hooks are middleware with next: next not called, what it guards doesn't happen (onWrite: no write, every table write: a value held back, its placement too; onRead: none shown; onTeardown: fn not run; onRecord: not held); next called with arguments changed, they go on changed (a write a hook changed names it in its metadata's features; an item onRead added names it in from.feature; onTeardown's why changed is what fn is told). a hook's own throw: a FeatureError naming the feature and the hook; a Refusal it throws stays a Refusal, the feature and hook named on it; a next's throw passing through the hooks above it as it is. hooks are setup-only (setup-only), places is made after setup (not-yet). reserveSlot: each feature's own state, by process context",
